@startuml RB-XXX
' ============================================================
' UC-XXX: <Use Case Title>
' Source: derived directly from UC-XXX use case text.
' Each numbered controller below corresponds to a sentence
' (or step) in the use case and will become a message on the
' sequence diagram and a test case in the test plan.
'
' Basic Course (mirror UC-XXX):
'   1 | <Actor name from UC> <action verb>
'     | System <response verb>
'   2 | <Actor name from UC> <action verb>
'     | System <response verb>
'
' Alternate Course A: <name>
'   A1 | <deviation user action>
'      | <deviation system response>
'
' Alternate Course B: <name>
'   B1 | <deviation user action>
'      | <deviation system response>
' ============================================================
' ICONIX connection rules:
'   Actor      <-> Boundary             OK
'   Boundary   <-> Controller           OK
'   Controller <-> Controller           OK
'   Controller <-> Entity               OK
' FORBIDDEN:
'   Actor      -> Controller / Entity   (must go via Boundary)
'   Boundary   -> Boundary              (must go via Controller)
'   Boundary   -> Entity                (must go via Controller)
'   Entity     -> Entity                (must go via Controller)
'
' NOTES:
' - UI sub-elements (buttons, fields, dropdowns, menu items) are
'   NOT boundaries -- only screens / pages / dialogs / API surfaces are.
' - Invoked UCs use a `usecase` node, NOT a `control`. See
'   `agents/iconix-analyst.md` `# Invoked use cases on robustness diagrams`.
' - Display vs Load: separate controllers when both happen. See
'   `agents/iconix-analyst.md` `# Display vs data-fetch controllers`.
'
' PLANTUML PLACEHOLDER NOTES:
' - Quoted element labels (between "...") render as literal text on the
'   diagram, including any < > characters inside. Replace them with the
'   real names from your UC.
' - Arrow labels (after the colon) MUST be plain text without < > -- bare
'   angle brackets there break PlantUML rendering. The placeholder labels
'   below use square brackets [like this] -- replace with real text.
' ============================================================

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

' --- Actors (use the actor names from the UC; no generic "User") ---
actor "<Actor name from UC>"   as Actor1
' actor "<Secondary actor>"    as Actor2

' --- Boundaries (named screens / pages / API surfaces from the UC) ---
' UI sub-elements (buttons, fields) are NOT boundaries -- only the parent page is.
boundary "<Page name>"          as PageA
' boundary "<Other page>"       as PageB

' --- UI dependencies: pages REUSED from another UC ---
' Same boundary syntax + `<<from PREFIX-UC-XXX Title>>` stereotype so the reuse
' is visible in M2 review. See agent's UI-dependencies rendering rule.
' boundary "<Reused page>" as ReusedPage <<from PREFIX-UC-XXX Other-UC-Title>>

' --- Entities (domain objects from the UC; refined from domain model) ---
entity "<DomainClass>"          as Ent1
' entity "<OtherDomainClass>"   as Ent2

' --- Downstream consumer actors (read async outputs of this UC) ---
' Drawn with a DASHED arrow (..>) from the produced entity to distinguish
' the async / decoupled handoff from this UC's synchronous flow.
' actor "<Consumer>"            as Consumer

' --- Invoked use cases (when this UC's flow invokes another UC). ---
' usecase nodes, NOT controllers. See agent rule.
' usecase "<Other UC Title>"    as OtherUC

' --- Controllers (one per logical system step in the UC) ---
control "<Verb-led action>"     as Step1
' Display step: presents a screen
control "Display <Page>"        as DisplayPage
' Separate fetch step when display + fetch are distinct
control "Load <Entity>"         as LoadData

' --- Alternate-course controllers (highlighted pink for visual contrast) ---
control "<Error / branch action>"   as AltStep1   #Pink

' -- Basic course wiring --
Actor1      --> PageA          : [action label]
PageA       --> Step1
Step1       --> Ent1           : [data passed]
Step1       --> DisplayPage
DisplayPage --> PageA

' -- Alternate course wiring --
Step1       --> AltStep1       : [branch condition]
AltStep1    --> PageA          : [recovery]

' -- Invoked use case (example -- delete if not applicable) --
' Step1     --> OtherUC        : [when invoked]
' OtherUC   --> Step1          : [after returning]

' -- UI dependency wiring (example -- delete if not applicable) --
' Step1     --> ReusedPage     : [when reused page is shown]

' -- Downstream consumer wiring (example -- delete if not applicable) --
' Note the DASHED arrow distinguishing async handoff.
' Ent1      ..> Consumer       : [downstream -- read by PREFIX-UC-XXX]

note bottom
  Traceability:
    UC: PREFIX-UC-XXX
    Upstream REQ(s): PREFIX-REQ-XXX
    Sequence diagram: PREFIX-SD-XXX (filled by Developer)
    Test cases: (filled by Tester)

    Replace PREFIX with the project prefix from iconix.config.yaml
    (e.g., BS-UC-001 for the Internet Bookstore worked example).
end note

@enduml
